Jahshaka local patch 0023 (upstream-reportable): the raster-fed IrradianceField
stores probe depths in WORLD units scaled by the probe COUNT, while the pixel
shader's Chebyshev visibility test compares them against PROBE-GRID distances.

IrradianceFieldRaster_piece_cs.any (CubemapToIfd) writes
`dist = dot( abs( linearDepth * samplingDir ), p_numProbes )` -- linearDepth is
in world units (projection params of the capture camera). The voxel path
(IrradianceFieldGenFromVct) multiplies a distance in the volume's [0,1] space by
numProbes, which IS grid units, and IrradianceField_piece_ps.any compares the
atlas against `length( probeOrigin - ifdGridPos )`, also grid units. So the
raster atlas is off by the field's size per axis: for any field larger than one
unit the stored depth dwarfs every cage distance, `r > mean` never fires, and
every probe reads as unoccluded -- the leak fix DDGI exists for is absent on the
raster path (Jahshaka: 32x8x32 probes over an 18x9x18 volume = 18x too far).

Fix: a new `invFieldSize` float3 param on the CubemapToIfd job (default 1,1,1,
which reproduces upstream's behaviour byte for byte) multiplied in, so a host
that sets it to 1 / the field's (enlarged) size per axis gets grid units.
Suggested upstream C++: IrradianceFieldRaster::createWorkspace sets it from
mCreator->mFieldSize beside mNumProbesParam. Jahshaka sets it host-side on the
shared job before every raster update (OgreGi.cpp, JahIrradianceField).

MEDIA-ONLY (Samples/Media/Compute/Algorithms/IrradianceFields/): no Ogre
rebuild, every tree runs the patch loop. Verified: `git apply --check` against
the pristine pin, `--reverse --check` after applying. Ledger: entry 23 in
irisgl/docs/OGRE_BUILD.md.

